Final Verdict

Your Live Migration Operations page already has a strong technical foundation and clearly demonstrates enterprise capability. However, it currently behaves more like an internal operations console than the flagship experience of a premium SaaS platform.

I would redesign it around three audiences simultaneously:

Security Engineers → Live operations, logs, rollback, telemetry, and migration controls.
SOC Managers → Progress, health, exceptions, and operational KPIs.
Executives/CISOs → Business outcomes, compliance, quantum readiness, risk reduction, and certification status.

The transformation should tell a clear story:

Discover → Analyze → Prioritize → Approve → Upgrade → Validate → Monitor → Certify

Rather than simply displaying jobs and logs, the dashboard should visually communicate that QGuard Helix is actively transforming an organization's entire cryptographic infrastructure from quantum-vulnerable technologies (RSA, ECC, TLS 1.2, legacy PKI) into a modern, NIST-compliant post-quantum security architecture. That narrative is what will differentiate QGuard Helix from traditional vulnerability management and cryptographic inventory tools, and it elevates the platform to the standard expected by Fortune 500 enterprises, government agencies, financial institutions, and critical infrastructure operators.